    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.13) leading the charge as our most confident start. His elite speed profile remains the cornerstone of our strategy, and facing a manageable arm like Luis Castillo (xERA 4.18), he profiles as a primary engine for our category scarcity needs. Joining him at the top of the board is **Trea Turner** (74.58) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.46), both of whom benefit from prime order positioning and favorable matchups against Janson Junk. The proximity to the top of the lineup for both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** maximizes their scoring ceilings, despite modest platoon adjustments. Additionally, **Caleb Durbin** (68.37) is an excellent play; the high xERA of Mitch Bratt (5.58) combined with favorable park factors elevates him significantly above his base projection, making him a high-efficiency utility option.\n\n**Junior Caminero** (70.15) remains a standout, as his power profile holds firm against Brandon Young. While **Colt Keith** (61.14) and **Carson Benge** (58.65) remain solid, we are monitoring the lineup stability for **Dillon Dingler** (46.17) and **Chase Meidroth** (45.68), both of whom are currently hovering near our \"marginal\" threshold. The closest decision of the day involved **Lars Nootbaar** (50.13); while his park factors are positive, a tough platoon draw against Alec Gamboa nearly pushed him to the bench. We ultimately kept him in play to capture his lead-off spot upside, preferring him over potential bench depth like **Nelson Velazquez** or **Casey Schmitt**, who lacked the structural advantages in the daily projection. \n\nRegarding risks, we are operating with a heavy \"Lineup Pending\" disclaimer for **Dillon Dingler**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Should any of these players drop in the batting order once confirmed lineups are released, their 